---
import {
  labAddonPrice,
  labPanelPrice,
  labStandalonePrice,
} from '../config';
---

<section id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div style="text-align:center">
      <span class="kicker">Questions mamas actually ask</span>
      <h2>Before you ask</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details
        ><summary>Is this a crash diet?</summary><p
          >The opposite. Your ranges are built to protect muscle and, if you're
          nursing, milk supply. Lose faster than your plan calls for and the app
          flags it, then Callie raises your food. We are firmly against
          1,200-calorie culture.</p
        ></details
      >
      <details
        ><summary>Can I do this while breastfeeding?</summary><p
          >Yes. Callie coaches supply-aware and your ranges account for nursing
          from day one. Under 3 months, it depends on how your body feels; some
          mamas are ready this early, and Callie confirms your ranges and timing
          herself before you start. <a href="/quiz">Get your macro ranges</a> anytime.</p
        ></details
      >
      <details
        ><summary>How much of Callie do I actually get?</summary><p
          >Callie personally reads your intake and builds your ranges. She's in
          the group coaching thread Monday through Friday, usually in voice
          notes, and her answers teach the whole group. You also get 1:1
          Messages and the Monday voice note every week. This is not a bot with
          her name on it.</p
        ></details
      >
      <details
        ><summary>Are there hidden costs? Shakes? Supplements?</summary><p
          >No. One price covers the full 8 weeks, the app, and the coaching. The
          food is real food from your regular grocery store, built around what
          your family already eats.</p
        ></details
      >
      <details
        ><summary>Do I need a gym?</summary><p
          >No. The daily rhythm works with walks, home strength, and whatever
          your season allows. Your ranges are built around your real activity,
          not an aspirational one.</p
        ></details
      >
      <details
        ><summary>Will I have to track food forever?</summary><p
          >No, and that's the point. Eight weeks of honest logging teaches you
          what your portions look like — so you can eyeball a plate without the
          app and get on with your life. That's the skill. You won't need the
          tracker forever.</p
        ></details
      >
      <details
        ><summary>What happens when I have a bad week?</summary><p
          >You will, and it's built in. Log it (you can log past days), tell
          Callie what happened, reset Monday. No shame spiral, no starting over
          from zero. The pattern over weeks matters more than any single day.</p
        ></details
      >
      <details
        ><summary>Do I have to be a mom, or postpartum?</summary><p
          >No. The coaching is postpartum-aware because that's where the worst
          advice lives, but any woman who wants ranges, real food, and a human
          coach is welcome.</p
        ></details
      >
      <details
        ><summary>Is this an App Store app?</summary><p
          >It's a web app you add to your home screen from the link we send.
          Same icon, same push notifications, nothing to download or update.
          About 20 seconds to set up, and we walk you through it.</p
        ></details
      >
      <details
        ><summary>What's the Lab Review add-on?</summary><p
          >An optional deep-dive for ${labAddonPrice}, added at enrollment or
          anytime during your 8 weeks. Callie, who is blood chemistry certified,
          personally reviews your bloodwork, records a voice memo walkthrough,
          answers your questions in Messages, and adjusts your ranges based on
          what your labs show. You can use recent lab results, order bloodwork
          through Callie for an additional ${labPanelPrice}, or get a panel
          through your GP, which insurance often covers. It's educational
          analysis, not medical diagnosis, and spots are limited to protect
          Callie's review time. Her standalone lab analysis is normally
          ${labStandalonePrice}.</p
        ></details
      >
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
